index a3c690c..3a35c5c 100644
--- a/docs/source/console.rst
+++ b/docs/source/console.rst
@@ -70,6 +70,16 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object to a string, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result as plain text followed by ``end``. Use it when you want the text written as-is.
+
+``out`` does not pretty print containers or objects, does not word wrap or crop the output, does not interpret markup, and does not replace emoji codes. It does apply highlighting by default (the ``highlight`` argument defaults to ``True``; pass ``None`` to use the console setting, or ``False`` to disable it), and it accepts a basic ``style`` argument. Output still goes through the normal print path, so render hooks and the console buffer are used as usual::
+
+    >>> console.out("[bold]not markup[/bold]", "foo", sep="-")
+
+
 Justify / Alignment
